Imports:
  - Types:
      - toBrandedType
    From: packages/common/src

Usages:
  branded_geometry_types: |
    Every geometric value (point, vector, line, segment, rectangle, triangle, polygon, curve,
    ellipse, angle-in-radians, angle-in-degrees) is a branded tuple/object type built with
    `toBrandedType`, distinct from a plain number/array/object of the same shape. A GlobalPoint
    (canvas/scene coordinates) and a LocalPoint (element-relative coordinates) are both
    [x, y] tuples at runtime but are different branded types, so a value from one coordinate
    space can't be silently passed where the other is expected. Always construct these via this
    cell's constructor functions (`pointFrom`, `vector`, `lineSegment`, rectangle, curve,
    ...), never via a bare literal.

Annotations: |
  Dependency-light 2D geometry primitives shared by the whole scene/element system: point and
  vector arithmetic, line/segment intersection and distance, cubic-bezier curve evaluation, and
  rectangle/polygon operations. Pure functions only — nothing here touches the DOM or React.

  Use `toBrandedType` (from Imports) and `branded_geometry_types` together when adding a new
  geometric type or constructor function.

---

"GlobalPoint()":
  location: point.ts
  annotations: |
    A branded [x, y] point in scene (canvas) coordinate space. See branded_geometry_types.

"LocalPoint()":
  location: point.ts
  annotations: |
    A branded [x, y] point in an individual element's local coordinate space. See
    branded_geometry_types.

"pointFrom(x: number, y: number) -> point:GlobalPoint | LocalPoint":
  location: point.ts
  annotations: |
    Construct a branded point from raw coordinates.

    `x`, `y`: raw coordinate values
    `point`: a new branded point (caller's generic parameter selects GlobalPoint vs LocalPoint)

    Use `branded_geometry_types` and `toBrandedType` for why this indirection exists instead of
    a plain tuple literal.

"pointDistance(a: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, b: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint) -> distance:number":
  location: point.ts
  annotations: |
    Euclidean distance between two points of the same coordinate space.

"pointRotateRads(point: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, center: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, angle: Radians) -> rotated:GlobalPoint | LocalPoint":
  location: point.ts
  annotations: |
    Rotate `point` around `center` by `angle` radians.

"vector(x: number, y: number, originX: number, originY: number) -> v:Vector":
  location: vector.ts
  annotations: |
    Construct a branded 2D vector [x - originX, y - originY].

"vectorFromPoint(p: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, origin: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint) -> v:Vector":
  location: vector.ts
  annotations: |
    Build the vector from `origin` to `p`.

"lineSegment(a: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, b: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint) -> segment:LineSegment":
  location: segment.ts
  annotations: |
    Construct a branded finite line segment between two points (as opposed to line, an
    infinite line through the same two points).

"segmentsIntersectAt(a: LineSegment, b: LineSegment) -> point:GlobalPoint | LocalPoint | null":
  location: segment.ts
  annotations: |
    Compute where two finite segments cross, or `null` if they don't intersect within their
    bounds.

"distanceToLineSegment(point: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, line: LineSegment) -> distance:number":
  location: segment.ts
  annotations: |
    Shortest distance from `point` to the closest point on segment line (0 if the point lies
    on the segment).

"rectangleIntersectRectangle(rectangle1: Rectangle, rectangle2: Rectangle) -> intersects:boolean":
  location: rectangle.ts
  annotations: |
    True if the two axis-aligned rectangles (each represented as two corner points) overlap.

"curveClosestPoint(c: Curve, p: GlobalPoint | LocalPoint, tolerance: number) -> point:GlobalPoint | LocalPoint | null":
  location: curve.ts
  annotations: |
    Find the point on cubic-bezier curve `c` closest to `p`, within `tolerance`, or `null` if
    none satisfies the tolerance.

"curveLength(c: Curve) -> length:number":
  location: curve.ts
  annotations: |
    Arc length of cubic-bezier curve `c`.

"rangeIntersection(a: InclusiveRange, b: InclusiveRange) -> overlap:InclusiveRange | null":
  location: range.ts
  annotations: |
    Intersection of two inclusive numeric ranges, or `null` if they don't overlap. Built via
    `toBrandedType` (from Imports) on the resulting [start, end] pair — the only place in this
    cell that reaches into packages/common/src at runtime.

"clamp(value: number, min: number, max: number) -> clamped:number":
  location: utils.ts
  annotations: |
    Constrain `value` to the closed interval [min, max].

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Pure 2D geometry primitives (points, vectors, lines, curves, rectangles, ranges) as branded
  types over plain tuples/objects. Depends only on packages/common/src's `toBrandedType`.
